WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:02.336
[♪ theme music playing]

00:24.316 --> 00:26.944
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

00:29.029 --> 00:30.739
ALL CHARACTERS, PLACES,
ORGANIZATIONS, ETC. ARE FICTIONAL

00:30.822 --> 00:32.032
CHILD ACTORS WERE FILMED
WITH GUARDIANS PRESENT

00:32.241 --> 00:33.951
ANIMALS WERE FILMED
UNDER EXPERT SUPERVISION AND WELFARE RULES

00:34.660 --> 00:35.702
Think carefully...

00:38.580 --> 00:39.957
if you want to protect your son.

00:43.418 --> 00:44.461
[Jessica] Promise me...

00:47.506 --> 00:48.924
Henry's safety.

00:49.883 --> 00:50.884
[breath trembling]

00:51.260 --> 00:52.344
Then,

00:53.762 --> 00:55.180
I'll give you what you want.

00:55.264 --> 00:56.682
[♪ tense, dramatic music playing]

01:03.272 --> 01:05.148
The proof that you conspired
with Jang Hangu.

01:06.858 --> 01:07.943
Where is it?

01:11.738 --> 01:12.823
At the vacation home.

01:14.658 --> 01:16.493
Henry's favorite plush toy is there.

01:18.370 --> 01:19.371
Inside that,

01:20.706 --> 01:22.666
you'll find the proof you need.

01:26.670 --> 01:27.713
On Jeju Island...

01:29.715 --> 01:31.216
I have a distant relative living there.

01:33.260 --> 01:34.261
Henry.

01:35.637 --> 01:36.680
Leave him with them.

01:38.640 --> 01:39.683
Keep your word.

01:49.484 --> 01:50.485
Wait.

01:50.569 --> 01:51.945
[♪ ominous music playing]

01:59.536 --> 02:01.705
[young Kim Wooju] Please help.

02:08.920 --> 02:10.839
-[glass shattering]
-[tires screeching]

02:16.094 --> 02:17.179
You...

02:18.305 --> 02:20.182
[breathing heavily]

02:35.155 --> 02:36.907
[slow, heavy breathing]

02:41.244 --> 02:42.996
[♪ music crescendos, fades]

02:44.873 --> 02:46.416
[panting]

02:48.543 --> 02:49.753
Mr. Kim!

02:50.379 --> 02:52.464
-[grunts]
-Are you all right?

02:56.134 --> 02:58.261
-[breathing heavily]
-You're okay.

02:58.345 --> 02:59.429
It's okay now.

03:01.181 --> 03:02.933
Hang on while I call 911.

03:03.016 --> 03:04.059
I'm fine.

03:04.476 --> 03:05.686
I took my medication.

03:07.479 --> 03:08.897
Forget that.

03:10.857 --> 03:11.900
Oh Minjeong.

03:12.609 --> 03:14.277
I think I know who she really is.

03:15.153 --> 03:16.697
[♪ soft, melancholy music playing]

03:22.160 --> 03:24.246
EPISODE 11

03:24.329 --> 03:25.622
I don't know why,

03:26.456 --> 03:28.250
but that night suddenly came to mind.

03:30.377 --> 03:31.837
The person I saw that day...

03:33.338 --> 03:34.548
I swear it was Oh Minjeong.

03:35.757 --> 03:37.384
Your memory should be correct.

03:39.219 --> 03:40.387
Ms. Oh...

03:41.763 --> 03:45.559
I heard she worked
at Myungsoondang 25 years ago.

03:47.394 --> 03:49.938
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

03:54.067 --> 03:55.986
That BQ Capital woman.

03:56.778 --> 03:59.364
[Sejung] Sylvia Oh? She was arrested.

03:59.448 --> 04:01.616
[Ms. Oh] She looked so familiar.

04:01.700 --> 04:03.994
I saw her when she visited last time,

04:04.077 --> 04:07.539
and I couldn't shake the feeling
I'd seen her somewhere.

04:07.622 --> 04:09.166
She was beautiful.

04:09.249 --> 04:11.084
That's how I remembered her.

04:11.877 --> 04:14.838
She was Ms. Oh
from the secretary's office.

04:15.422 --> 04:17.757
-She was a Miss Korea participant.
-[Sejung] Ms. Oh...

04:19.009 --> 04:21.011
It's possible that's when she started...

04:21.094 --> 04:25.348
Or maybe she knew Director Jang
long before that.

04:28.018 --> 04:30.312
She could've also been
at the scene of your accident.

04:31.688 --> 04:32.731
Oh Minjeong said

04:34.065 --> 04:37.027
there's a phone at the vacation home
that she uses to contact my uncle.

04:39.488 --> 04:41.490
I think that will be the smoking gun.

04:41.865 --> 04:43.784
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

04:45.952 --> 04:48.205
PHONE RECORDINGS

04:54.961 --> 04:56.338
[mouse clicking]

05:00.967 --> 05:03.929
[Jessica] The president
found out about us.

05:04.304 --> 05:05.430
What do we do?

05:05.514 --> 05:07.098
[Hangu] We need to get rid of him.

05:07.182 --> 05:09.017
-[Jessica] What?
-[Hangu] There's a family gathering

05:09.100 --> 05:10.268
in Yeosu next week.

05:10.352 --> 05:13.188
That's when we'll have to get it done.

05:14.648 --> 05:16.191
[♪ music increases in tempo]

05:20.862 --> 05:22.489
[whistling tune]

05:49.474 --> 05:50.684
Was it you, Uncle?

05:54.479 --> 05:55.522
Tell me.

05:57.816 --> 05:59.192
Was it you?

06:00.569 --> 06:01.570
[scoffs]

06:02.487 --> 06:05.615
What a shame. You heard it all. [scoffs]

06:06.283 --> 06:08.785
[inhales deeply] What should I say?

06:09.411 --> 06:11.496
Should I say it's a relief you found out?

06:11.580 --> 06:14.958
Or should I say,
"What can you do about it now?"

06:16.418 --> 06:19.504
Man, it's really hard to say. [chuckles]

06:20.255 --> 06:22.883
There are things
you're better off not knowing.

06:22.966 --> 06:25.260
You'd prefer it if I didn't know.

06:25.343 --> 06:26.720
[scoffs] No.

06:27.429 --> 06:30.348
When you know the truth
but can't do anything about it...

06:30.432 --> 06:31.808
Nothing's more miserable than that.

06:31.892 --> 06:33.393
I can't do anything about it?

06:33.476 --> 06:38.607
The statute of limitations for that case
expired in July 2015.

06:38.690 --> 06:40.358
[♪ ominous music playing]

06:41.026 --> 06:43.111
Now you know I killed your parents,

06:43.778 --> 06:45.822
but you can't do anything about it.

06:47.866 --> 06:49.367
[sighs dismissively]

06:52.829 --> 06:55.040
You're still the poor boy you always were.

06:55.874 --> 06:58.293
No, I bet you feel even worse now.

06:58.918 --> 07:00.837
"I'd be better off not knowing."

07:02.047 --> 07:03.381
[laughs maliciously]

07:05.717 --> 07:08.345
You'll hate your helpless, powerless self.

07:10.263 --> 07:11.306
You...

07:13.099 --> 07:15.810
simply took their lives
because he knew of your affair?

07:15.894 --> 07:17.771
No, it wasn't because he'd found out.

07:17.854 --> 07:20.148
It was because he had ruined my plan.

07:24.653 --> 07:26.988
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

07:36.581 --> 07:38.291
I'll tell my father.

07:38.375 --> 07:39.834
Resign and walk away.

07:40.877 --> 07:42.796
Don't even dream of getting alimony.

07:44.589 --> 07:46.466
[anxiously] I'm so very sorry.

07:46.883 --> 07:48.760
Forgive me this one time
for Miyeon's sake.

07:49.552 --> 07:52.430
She threatened self-harm to marry me.

07:53.723 --> 07:55.767
[crying] She can't raise Eungsoo
on her own.

07:56.184 --> 07:58.645
You slept with a secretary knowing that?

07:58.728 --> 08:01.231
It won't happen ever again.

08:01.606 --> 08:02.649
Please.

08:03.316 --> 08:05.276
For Miyeon's sake!

08:06.569 --> 08:08.530
-[exclaims in frustration]
-[breath trembling]

08:09.531 --> 08:11.408
-[sighs]
-[breathing heavily]

08:11.741 --> 08:13.660
[Hangu] I got married
with a dream mapped out.

08:13.993 --> 08:15.954
How dare he ruin that for me?

08:16.037 --> 08:17.539
You asked him for forgiveness,

08:19.332 --> 08:20.709
but then killed my parents?

08:22.252 --> 08:23.420
With Oh Minjeong?

08:23.503 --> 08:24.587
What else could I do?

08:25.213 --> 08:28.299
He could use my weakness
against me at any time.

08:32.554 --> 08:33.680
See?

08:35.390 --> 08:37.559
You didn't have to know the truth.

08:37.642 --> 08:39.436
[♪ music increases in tempo]

08:39.519 --> 08:41.020
[laughs smugly]

09:02.584 --> 09:03.835
What's this about? What's going on?

09:03.918 --> 09:05.003
[detective 1] Mr. Jang Hangu.

09:05.462 --> 09:08.423
You're under arrest for defrauding
and embezzling from Myungsoondang.

09:08.798 --> 09:11.051
There seems to be a misunderstanding.

09:11.134 --> 09:13.553
I was questioned,
and no charges were filed against me.

09:13.636 --> 09:14.679
[detective 2] David Lee.

09:14.763 --> 09:16.139
He was arrested in a gambling den.

09:16.222 --> 09:18.141
-What?
-On his phone,

09:18.224 --> 09:19.601
we found proof that he,

09:19.684 --> 09:22.437
alongside you and Oh Minjeong,
conspired in a fake Kaltz Hotel deal.

09:23.521 --> 09:25.690
I'll come with you to explain that.

09:26.649 --> 09:28.276
Add conspiring to commit murder.

09:30.320 --> 09:31.905
He conspired with Oh Minjeong

09:32.489 --> 09:33.782
and killed my parents.

09:34.407 --> 09:36.117
[detective 1] What?
Conspiracy to commit murder?

09:36.493 --> 09:38.286
The statutes to that have expired.

09:38.369 --> 09:39.412
[Kim Wooju] No.

09:40.914 --> 09:41.998
They haven't expired.

09:45.293 --> 09:46.795
[♪ tense, dramatic music playing]

10:03.269 --> 10:04.729
While you were abroad for a week,

10:05.021 --> 10:07.690
I destroyed the security footage
of the hit-and-run.

10:08.483 --> 10:10.110
The case will be closed

10:11.569 --> 10:12.821
due to a lack of evidence.

10:17.909 --> 10:19.119
Good job, Detective Kim.

10:21.579 --> 10:22.997
[grunts] Here.

10:36.386 --> 10:37.846
[chuckles softly]

10:43.852 --> 10:45.728
This is the dash cam footage

10:45.812 --> 10:47.897
from April 28, 2009 from this man's car.

10:47.981 --> 10:49.149
[mouse clicks]

10:50.316 --> 10:52.068
[Det. Kim] While you were abroad
for a week,

10:52.152 --> 10:54.696
I destroyed the security footage
of the hit-and-run.

10:54.779 --> 10:57.448
[Kim Wooju] Jang Hangu
fled abroad for a week

10:58.116 --> 11:00.285
while he was being questioned
about a hit-and-run.

11:00.368 --> 11:01.494
A hit-and-run?

11:01.578 --> 11:04.914
He bribed a detective
to destroy the security footage

11:04.998 --> 11:06.457
and was released on lack of evidence.

11:06.541 --> 11:08.418
What on earth are you talking about?

11:08.501 --> 11:11.880
The statute of limitations was extended
for the week you were abroad,

11:11.963 --> 11:14.048
and that means
you can still be prosecuted.

11:14.799 --> 11:16.676
[stutters] No, that can't be.

11:16.759 --> 11:18.261
The audio was faked!

11:18.344 --> 11:19.804
I never did anything of the sort!

11:19.888 --> 11:22.682
There's proof of the conspiracy
in his jacket pocket.

11:29.772 --> 11:31.191
[♪ music crescendos]

11:34.360 --> 11:35.445
[detective 1] Mr. Jang Hangu.

11:35.528 --> 11:38.031
We'll add a conspiracy of murder
to the charges.

11:38.114 --> 11:39.240
-Cuff him.
-Okay.

11:41.367 --> 11:44.871
You have the right to an attorney,
the right to remain silent,

11:44.954 --> 11:46.706
and to request a review of your arrest.

11:46.789 --> 11:48.708
No way. Why bring up the past?

11:48.791 --> 11:50.084
-[detective 1] Take him.
-Let me go.

11:50.168 --> 11:51.669
Let go of me!

11:52.045 --> 11:53.213
[Hangu grunts]

11:53.838 --> 11:54.964
Wooju, you...

11:55.048 --> 11:56.299
[Hangu yelps]

11:58.968 --> 12:00.011
[sirens wailing]

12:02.889 --> 12:04.557
[♪ music increases in tempo]

12:06.851 --> 12:08.102
[exhales sharply]

12:17.904 --> 12:20.823
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

12:25.954 --> 12:27.163
[bailiff] All rise.

12:40.969 --> 12:42.303
[bailiff] Please be seated.

12:45.682 --> 12:47.642
We'll begin the trial.

12:48.518 --> 12:51.813
Case number 2025-KO-182.

12:51.896 --> 12:54.023
I'll read the sentence.

12:54.107 --> 12:55.358
Defendant Jang Hangu

12:56.025 --> 12:59.487
planned a long-term con
to take control of Myungsoondang.

12:59.988 --> 13:03.032
He put together
a 30-billion-won investment fraud.

13:03.574 --> 13:08.788
In the process, he illegally obtained
Kim Miyeon's Hawaii property,

13:08.871 --> 13:12.083
used J Consulting to embezzle funds,

13:12.166 --> 13:14.669
and conspired
with Oh Minjeong and David Lee

13:14.752 --> 13:18.631
to deceive the victim
with a forged Kaltz Hotel contract,

13:19.132 --> 13:22.635
hereby causing grievous monetary loss.

13:22.719 --> 13:26.222
We also acknowledge that he turned
the fraud victim into the assailant,

13:26.889 --> 13:29.142
damaging Myungsoondang's credibility,

13:29.767 --> 13:33.479
brand image,
and obstructing their business.

13:33.563 --> 13:34.897
Take this.

13:34.981 --> 13:36.107
The chairwoman gave it to me.

13:36.190 --> 13:37.817
-I had too many.
-[judge] In addition to that,

13:37.900 --> 13:42.363
to murder Ko Seongtae, who found
J Consulting's padded account ledger,

13:42.447 --> 13:45.074
he paid his driver, Lee Janghun,
to commit murder.

13:45.950 --> 13:48.119
He also conspired
with Lee Janghun and Oh Minjeong

13:48.202 --> 13:52.707
to poison Ko Philnyun multiple times.

13:54.667 --> 13:56.210
Finally, in around 2009,

13:56.711 --> 14:00.173
the statute of limitations on the charges
of a hit-and-run resulting in bodily harm

14:00.256 --> 14:03.426
and bribery expired,
and he can no longer be prosecuted.

14:03.509 --> 14:08.389
However, he fled abroad
to avoid criminal prosecution,

14:08.890 --> 14:11.476
and that's serious enough
to extend the statute.

14:11.559 --> 14:13.936
In July 27, 2000,

14:14.020 --> 14:16.355
the defendant conspired
with accomplice Oh Minjeong

14:16.439 --> 14:20.026
and murdered Kim Useok and Lee Eunyeong
in a car crash disguised as an accident.

14:20.651 --> 14:23.780
Under ordinary circumstances, the statute
of limitations would've expired,

14:23.863 --> 14:28.826
but the court will discount the time
the defendant fled abroad,

14:28.910 --> 14:31.245
and that means he can be prosecuted.

14:32.663 --> 14:36.292
Based on the accomplice's confession
and the objective evidence,

14:36.375 --> 14:40.254
the court finds him guilty of the murder
of Kim Useok and Lee Eunyeong.

14:40.338 --> 14:42.340
-[spectators gasp]
-No!

14:42.423 --> 14:43.841
No way!

14:43.925 --> 14:45.468
-That's nonsense!
-[judge] In conclusion,

14:45.551 --> 14:47.595
the defendant committed fraud,

14:47.678 --> 14:50.181
embezzlement, dereliction of duty,
obstruction of business,

14:50.264 --> 14:52.683
conspiracy to murder and murder.

14:52.767 --> 14:54.352
The nature of the crime
is extremely egregious,

14:54.435 --> 14:56.354
and its social harm is substantial.

14:56.437 --> 14:59.148
Accordingly, this court hereby grants
Jang Hangu, the defendant

15:00.066 --> 15:01.818
the death penalty.

15:02.401 --> 15:03.778
[♪ tense, dramatic music playing]

15:09.742 --> 15:10.743
[sighing in despair]

15:16.082 --> 15:17.542
[breathing heavily]

15:23.464 --> 15:25.007
You know, Mom.

15:28.302 --> 15:30.513
I couldn't go to court today.

15:32.974 --> 15:35.184
I didn't think I could face him.

15:36.811 --> 15:38.146
He ruined our family

15:39.438 --> 15:41.357
and killed Useok.

15:41.983 --> 15:45.987
I should beat him to death
for what he did to you on top of that.

15:47.405 --> 15:48.614
[♪ soft melancholy music playing]

15:50.449 --> 15:56.038
How did he manage to dupe me
for all those years?

16:04.338 --> 16:08.968
I didn't know what he was doing
so I whined and pestered you.

16:12.138 --> 16:15.308
[sobbing] I deserve to die.

16:18.227 --> 16:21.689
What should I do, Mom? What now?

16:23.608 --> 16:25.443
[Miyeon continues sobbing]

16:27.069 --> 16:29.030
GRAVE OF LEE EUNYEONG

16:39.123 --> 16:40.958
GRAVE OF KIM USEOK

16:53.888 --> 16:54.972
[sighs wearily]

16:59.143 --> 17:00.186
Mother, Father.

17:04.398 --> 17:05.524
It's all over now.

17:07.902 --> 17:09.779
[♪ poignant, melancholy music playing]

17:16.494 --> 17:17.620
[sniffles]

17:20.206 --> 17:21.249
Wooju.

17:21.958 --> 17:23.000
It was tough, wasn't it?

17:24.377 --> 17:25.419
Yes.

17:29.674 --> 17:31.801
[Useok] You were a cheeky boy
who wanted to do so many things.

17:32.343 --> 17:36.180
It made me sad to see you
huddled up in a corner.

17:39.517 --> 17:41.644
You got out of the long tunnel
on your own.

17:44.188 --> 17:45.231
I'm proud of you.

17:46.774 --> 17:47.858
From now on,

17:48.943 --> 17:51.779
let everything go and be happy.

17:53.197 --> 17:54.240
Can you do that?

17:55.783 --> 17:56.826
Yes.

17:57.118 --> 17:58.202
Good.

17:58.286 --> 17:59.620
[wailing]

18:01.247 --> 18:02.290
[Useok crying] My dear son.

18:03.082 --> 18:04.500
Daddy's so sorry.

18:08.588 --> 18:10.423
[young Kim Wooju continues wailing]

18:38.200 --> 18:40.453
Say hi to my parents.

18:42.538 --> 18:43.748
Hello.

18:44.332 --> 18:45.541
I'm Yoo Meri.

18:46.876 --> 18:49.378
I brought her to introduce her to you.

18:51.756 --> 18:53.215
Mother, Father.

18:54.550 --> 18:56.469
Don't worry too much anymore.

18:57.928 --> 19:01.515
I'll look after him
and make sure he's happy.

19:02.516 --> 19:04.310
[♪ gentle orchestral music playing]

19:42.390 --> 19:47.269
[Jingyeong] You know, people aren't really
interested in how you've lived.

19:47.353 --> 19:50.314
So, stop acting all guilty like that.

19:57.363 --> 19:58.572
[doorbell chimes]

20:01.575 --> 20:03.202
[pellets rattle in bottle,
places on table]

20:03.285 --> 20:04.286
[door beeps]

20:13.170 --> 20:14.213
[sighs softly]

20:15.840 --> 20:16.841
[door closes, beeps]

20:20.928 --> 20:21.971
Take a seat.

20:28.811 --> 20:29.854
What's this about?

20:36.360 --> 20:37.528
I feel terrible

20:38.612 --> 20:40.030
to have to tell you this.

20:42.533 --> 20:46.370
I don't think we can accept
the house that I won through the raffle.

20:48.289 --> 20:50.708
We're not actually a married couple.

20:50.791 --> 20:52.209
[♪ soft, melancholy music playing]

20:52.293 --> 20:56.422
My ex and I had agreed to divorce
around the time I won the unit.

20:56.797 --> 20:59.175
I didn't want to lose out on the prize,

21:00.009 --> 21:05.139
so I brought him to claim it with me
instead of a real husband.

21:05.681 --> 21:08.017
[Kim Wooju] We had
many opportunities to come clean,

21:08.601 --> 21:10.728
but we put it off due to my circumstances.

21:11.729 --> 21:14.899
We disrupted an important event
for your department store,

21:14.982 --> 21:18.861
and I'm willing pay for that
and for breaking the contract.

21:23.073 --> 21:24.283
[sighs]

21:31.832 --> 21:34.126
I feel relieved and free
now that I came clean,

21:35.211 --> 21:36.545
but Mr. Baek's reaction...

21:37.379 --> 21:40.674
I don't know. He didn't seem surprised.

21:40.758 --> 21:42.009
You know he has a straight face.

21:42.802 --> 21:44.678
He'll talk to his people
and get back to us.

21:44.762 --> 21:45.805
Let's wait.

21:47.139 --> 21:50.434
[sighs in relief]
We had a long day today, didn't we?

21:50.518 --> 21:52.394
We took care of something big.

21:54.104 --> 21:55.105
[sighs]

21:55.523 --> 21:58.192
Where will you move to?

21:58.776 --> 22:01.654
I'll move into Sori's studio apartment
and share the rent.

22:01.737 --> 22:02.863
Isn't that too far?

22:02.947 --> 22:04.323
It's a short ride on the subway.

22:04.406 --> 22:06.450
One hour isn't a short ride.

22:06.534 --> 22:08.077
It is to people like us.

22:08.619 --> 22:10.246
Oh, and I'll take driving lessons, too.

22:10.329 --> 22:11.413
You'll what?

22:11.497 --> 22:13.207
You can't. It's too dangerous.

22:13.290 --> 22:14.583
I'll drive you around.

22:15.501 --> 22:16.877
I'll just sleep less.

22:16.961 --> 22:18.003
[chuckles softly]

22:19.713 --> 22:23.676
It feels weird to think
I'm leaving this place.

22:24.927 --> 22:25.928
Of course.

22:26.011 --> 22:27.888
I love the walking trails here.

22:28.681 --> 22:30.266
Shall we go for a stroll, then?

22:32.017 --> 22:33.394
[Kim Wooju chuckles softly]

22:39.275 --> 22:40.818
[panting]

22:42.695 --> 22:43.946
[grunting]

22:48.617 --> 22:50.786
[panting] Revenge.

22:51.412 --> 22:52.913
Revenge!

22:52.997 --> 22:54.582
[♪ gripping, dramatic music playing]

22:55.374 --> 22:58.043
Revenge requires energy.

22:58.127 --> 22:59.461
Revenge.

23:00.004 --> 23:01.171
[exclaiming scornfully]

23:01.255 --> 23:03.507
Just you wait. [continues panting]

23:15.936 --> 23:16.979
I can do this.

23:19.940 --> 23:20.941
I can do this.

23:21.317 --> 23:22.318
I can do this.

23:26.196 --> 23:28.490
[grunts] I can...

23:28.574 --> 23:30.868
I can't do it. I can't. [exclaims]

23:30.951 --> 23:32.369
[panting]

23:33.120 --> 23:34.163
No.

23:35.205 --> 23:37.583
This is me taking a break.

23:37.666 --> 23:40.210
I'm taking one step back
to take two steps forward.

23:43.422 --> 23:45.049
Damn it!

23:47.968 --> 23:49.553
[grunting, panting]

24:03.025 --> 24:05.152
Why won't any of the companies
I applied to call me back?

24:07.947 --> 24:09.949
There's no way
they don't like my qualifications.

24:19.041 --> 24:21.210
MYUNGSOONDANG CLEARED OF FRAUD,
BACK IN BUSINESS

24:21.293 --> 24:22.753
[♪ tense, dramatic music playing]

24:24.213 --> 24:26.173
MYUNGSOONDANG RECOVERS CREDIBILITY
AND AIMS TO REGAIN FAVOR

24:26.256 --> 24:27.383
[breath trembling]

24:28.008 --> 24:31.762
I thought Kim Wooju would've fallen
by now, but he hasn't.

24:41.689 --> 24:42.731
Just wait.

24:44.400 --> 24:45.859
I'm still here.

24:45.943 --> 24:47.528
[♪ music crescendos, fades]

24:49.196 --> 24:50.739
[heart monitor beeps steadily]

24:54.952 --> 24:56.203
Blink for me.

25:04.169 --> 25:05.879
Can you grip my hand tight?

25:12.720 --> 25:13.971
She regained her consciousness.

25:14.430 --> 25:16.682
I'll need to take another MRI to be sure,

25:16.765 --> 25:18.267
-but she's responding just fine.
-[Eungsoo sighs in relief]

25:18.350 --> 25:19.643
[sighs in relief, chuckles]

25:21.061 --> 25:22.187
Mom.

25:22.646 --> 25:24.898
Mom, do you hear me?

25:24.982 --> 25:26.692
Can you recognize me, Mom?

25:27.651 --> 25:28.652
[sighs in relief]

25:28.736 --> 25:33.615
I was so scared you'd leave me all alone.

25:36.952 --> 25:39.288
She's talking. She wants to speak.
[chuckles]

25:39.371 --> 25:40.873
What is it, Mom?

25:42.082 --> 25:44.877
Keep your mouth shut.

25:44.960 --> 25:46.336
"Keep your mouth shut."

25:47.004 --> 25:48.380
My head's ringing.

25:48.464 --> 25:49.548
"My head's ringing."

25:51.800 --> 25:53.510
Don't repeat what we all heard.

25:54.219 --> 25:55.679
Come on, Mom.

25:55.763 --> 25:57.139
[all chuckling]

25:57.222 --> 25:58.766
[♪ soft, gentle music playing]

26:12.780 --> 26:13.906
[Meri over phone] What, really?

26:14.615 --> 26:16.283
That's such a relief.

26:17.284 --> 26:19.036
Everyone says she was incredibly lucky.

26:20.120 --> 26:23.165
[sighs] My eyes teared up
when she woke up.

26:24.124 --> 26:25.459
I almost cried.

26:26.001 --> 26:27.878
You're a crybaby.

26:29.004 --> 26:31.340
We can have dinner some other time.

26:31.423 --> 26:33.425
You should be with her today.

26:33.509 --> 26:34.551
[Kim Wooju] Okay.

26:34.635 --> 26:37.012
You can visit
once she regains some energy.

26:38.931 --> 26:39.973
Bye.

26:45.020 --> 26:46.021
[sighs in relief]

26:51.110 --> 26:52.152
Wooju.

26:57.449 --> 26:58.492
So... [clears throat]

27:02.412 --> 27:03.455
My husband...

27:05.749 --> 27:06.792
I mean...

27:07.251 --> 27:09.711
That fool.
The money he stole from the company.

27:10.838 --> 27:14.049
I'll get it back from him somehow.

27:15.217 --> 27:17.136
Give me a little time.

27:18.053 --> 27:21.723
Before that,
you should look after yourself first.

27:23.058 --> 27:25.060
Eungsoo has been really worried.

27:25.143 --> 27:27.437
He says you barely sleep at night.

27:34.236 --> 27:35.988
[sniffles] Well, that...

27:36.071 --> 27:37.197
[chuckles softly]

27:37.281 --> 27:40.075
That's because I'm menopausal.

27:41.326 --> 27:46.582
I don't have the right to complain
or say I'm having a hard time around you.

27:47.207 --> 27:50.168
I could make no excuses
even if I had extra mouths to speak with.

27:54.047 --> 27:55.966
You didn't know about it, either.

28:02.472 --> 28:03.557
I'm sorry, Wooju. [crying]

28:03.640 --> 28:05.392
[♪ soft, melancholy music playing]

28:05.851 --> 28:12.107
I gave you such a hard time,
and I left you alone for so long.

28:13.442 --> 28:15.319
There's no turning back time.

28:16.153 --> 28:20.449
If you don't want to see me ever again,

28:20.532 --> 28:22.492
we don't have to. [sniffles]

28:22.826 --> 28:25.495
If you don't want to call me "Auntie,"
then don't, okay?

28:25.579 --> 28:26.622
Until...

28:27.748 --> 28:32.002
Until you no longer feel resentful,
you can do whatever you want.

28:32.961 --> 28:34.004
Auntie.

28:35.839 --> 28:38.967
Just be there for me as you always were.

28:40.093 --> 28:42.846
I have no more family if I lose you, too.

28:45.474 --> 28:46.558
Wooju... [sobbing]

29:04.201 --> 29:05.243
[sniffles]

29:09.706 --> 29:11.458
[whistling]

29:12.918 --> 29:14.002
[in English] Okay.

29:16.964 --> 29:18.006
[in Korean] The plates.

29:18.423 --> 29:20.175
[in sing-song voice]
Everything must be straightened out.

29:20.759 --> 29:23.220
Lay out the plates.

29:23.303 --> 29:25.305
SEJUNG

29:26.056 --> 29:27.057
[exclaims]

29:29.142 --> 29:31.103
Hey, Sejung. Are you nearby?

29:31.186 --> 29:32.229
Yes.

29:33.188 --> 29:34.272
[Wonseok] Where are you?

29:36.191 --> 29:37.275
We're at the supermarket.

29:37.359 --> 29:38.694
The supermarket?

29:38.777 --> 29:40.779
-Do you need anything?
-You don't need to shop.

29:40.862 --> 29:44.199
Hey, it's a housewarming.
We can't go empty-handed.

29:44.491 --> 29:45.534
Drinks.

29:46.410 --> 29:47.411
Do you have drinks?

29:48.286 --> 29:49.621
Oh, really?

29:49.705 --> 29:51.164
Okay, see you later, then.

29:53.125 --> 29:55.085
Ms. Yoo said she'd get the alcohol.

29:55.168 --> 29:56.211
Oh, really?

29:56.837 --> 29:59.131
Should we get some toilet paper, then?

29:59.214 --> 30:00.257
-Sure.
-Where is it?

30:00.340 --> 30:01.383
It's over there.

30:01.758 --> 30:02.968
For his life to unravel well?

30:03.677 --> 30:06.263
-Shall we get some necessities?
-No, I'm sure he has enough.

30:06.346 --> 30:07.848
[♪ upbeat, whimsical music playing]

30:11.101 --> 30:12.561
That's a dreadful mix.

30:16.857 --> 30:17.858
[sighs]

30:20.360 --> 30:22.904
A box of peaches
on top of a box of grapes?

30:22.988 --> 30:25.157
Even numbers are always better than odd.

30:25.240 --> 30:26.283
What?

30:28.285 --> 30:30.078
-This is too much.
-A guy

30:30.537 --> 30:33.081
who lives alone never buys fruit.

30:33.165 --> 30:35.208
But fruit goes bad really quickly.
[chuckles]

30:35.292 --> 30:37.085
He can't eat all this on his own.

30:37.169 --> 30:38.420
It's fine.

30:38.503 --> 30:39.755
This is a pineapple.

30:39.838 --> 30:42.299
It's not a cactus. Don't sit on it.
[chuckles]

30:42.799 --> 30:43.800
[chuckles awkwardly]

30:44.634 --> 30:47.054
Seriously, stop. That's more than enough.

30:47.137 --> 30:48.805
You buy way too much.

30:50.098 --> 30:51.141
Fine.

30:52.142 --> 30:53.185
[clears throat]

30:56.980 --> 30:58.023
Mr. Kim.

30:58.523 --> 31:00.442
-Are you sulking?
-I'm not.

31:00.525 --> 31:02.778
-You are sulking.
-I'm not.

31:03.153 --> 31:04.529
Okay, buy everything you want.

31:04.613 --> 31:05.655
Can I really?

31:06.573 --> 31:07.783
Don't we also need this?

31:09.576 --> 31:12.162
-[groaning]
-[chuckles]

31:12.245 --> 31:15.332
I think my heart is melting.
[groans, chuckles]

31:15.999 --> 31:17.125
Hey.

31:17.209 --> 31:18.251
Over there.

31:19.795 --> 31:20.796
[gasps]

31:21.296 --> 31:23.715
Shall we say hi?
We'll see them later anyway.

31:23.799 --> 31:25.008
No, we can't. Not yet.

31:25.092 --> 31:27.427
I haven't told Songhee about us.

31:28.011 --> 31:29.805
-[Sejung] Anything else?
-Let's buy some fruit.

31:29.888 --> 31:32.307
-Hurry. Walk backward.
-Oh, but...

31:38.438 --> 31:40.315
-[Wonseok] Thank you all for coming!
-[all] Cheers!

31:40.398 --> 31:41.650
Freeze!

31:41.733 --> 31:43.610
-[Ms. Oh] Hurry up.
-[camera shutter clicks]

31:43.693 --> 31:45.487
-I'm done.
-[all] At last.

31:48.698 --> 31:50.575
[all exclaim]

31:51.576 --> 31:53.745
[sighs] That was almost sweet.

31:53.829 --> 31:56.706
Why? Are you under a lot of stress?

31:57.541 --> 31:58.667
Whose fault is that?

31:59.793 --> 32:00.877
Don't be like that.

32:00.961 --> 32:04.548
She's just upset
her blind date didn't work out.

32:04.631 --> 32:05.924
Right?

32:08.760 --> 32:09.803
What?

32:10.554 --> 32:11.972
[grunts] This won't do.

32:12.055 --> 32:14.266
It's time to open the Door of Truth.
Mr. Han?

32:14.349 --> 32:15.392
Spin.

32:15.475 --> 32:17.769
Will you make some space in the center?

32:19.563 --> 32:21.231
-[Wonseok] Ready?
-[Ms. Oh] Ready.

32:21.314 --> 32:23.316
Here goes the Door of Truth.

32:23.400 --> 32:24.442
[Ms. Oh] Spin!

32:25.777 --> 32:27.320
[all exclaim]

32:27.404 --> 32:28.446
What the heck?

32:29.114 --> 32:30.157
[Wonseok] Your question is,

32:30.240 --> 32:34.327
I'm stressed out
because of my blind date, yes or no?

32:35.871 --> 32:37.664
-No.
-See?

32:37.747 --> 32:39.374
-It's not the date.
-[Songhee] It's you.

32:39.457 --> 32:41.042
She didn't say it was because of me.

32:41.126 --> 32:42.377
[Wonseok] She might as well have.

32:42.460 --> 32:43.670
Okay, who's next?

32:43.753 --> 32:45.172
-Are you ready?
-[Ms. Oh] Yes.

32:48.925 --> 32:50.260
[all exclaim]

32:50.343 --> 32:52.429
-[Wonseok] Mr. Kim.
-[Sejung and Songhee] Mr. Kim.

32:52.554 --> 32:53.597
[Sejung] I have...

32:55.432 --> 32:56.558
a girlfriend, yes or no?

32:56.641 --> 32:58.351
[all mimicking drum roll]

33:01.646 --> 33:03.106
Do I have a girlfriend?

33:03.565 --> 33:05.400
-I do.
-[all gasp in awe]

33:05.483 --> 33:06.568
[Ms. Oh] What did I tell you?

33:06.651 --> 33:07.986
-[Sejung] He's dating.
-I told you so.

33:08.570 --> 33:10.071
-Do I spin? [clears throat]
-[Ms. Oh] Yes.

33:13.992 --> 33:15.744
[all cheering]

33:16.203 --> 33:18.455
-[Songhee] It's Ms. Yoo!
-[Ms. Oh] Ms. Yoo.

33:18.538 --> 33:21.666
[clears throat] I have a boyfriend,

33:21.750 --> 33:23.126
yes or no?

33:23.543 --> 33:25.170
[all mimicking drum roll]

33:26.421 --> 33:27.464
The answer is...

33:28.673 --> 33:29.716
I'll drink.

33:29.799 --> 33:31.968
-[Songhee] What?
-[Sejung] That's no fun.

33:32.052 --> 33:33.553
[Ms. Oh] That's not much of a secret.

33:33.637 --> 33:35.430
-Come on.
-[Sejung] Ms. Yoo...

33:35.513 --> 33:36.765
Let's all have a drink.

33:36.848 --> 33:38.600
-[Wonseok] Okay.
-[Sejung] Cheers. Let's drink.

33:38.683 --> 33:40.852
[Kim Wooju scoffs] This is what you'll do?

33:44.105 --> 33:45.482
[all exclaim]

33:45.565 --> 33:46.942
-[Wonseok] Ms. Yoo.
-[Ms. Oh] Ms. Yoo.

33:47.025 --> 33:50.195
I'm willing to go on a blind date,

33:50.278 --> 33:51.321
yes or no?

33:51.404 --> 33:52.572
[all mimicking drum roll]

33:52.656 --> 33:54.115
[Kim Wooju] She'd better say no.

33:55.450 --> 33:57.452
-I'll drink.
-[all exclaim]

33:57.535 --> 33:59.162
-[Sejung] This is no fun.
-[Songhee] What?

33:59.246 --> 34:00.789
[Wonseok] I'm full from trying to keep up.

34:00.872 --> 34:02.791
[Sejung] What if she drinks all the beer?

34:02.874 --> 34:05.252
-How many bottles...
-[Ms. Oh] What's up with her today?

34:05.794 --> 34:06.920
[exclaims]

34:07.837 --> 34:09.381
[Sejung] Let's keep going for Meri.

34:09.923 --> 34:11.258
-She's next.
-[Wonseok] It's time.

34:11.341 --> 34:13.051
-[Sejung] It's slowing down.
-[Ms. Oh] Let's go.

34:13.134 --> 34:15.762
-[Sejung] It's Ms. Yoo again.
-Ms. Yoo!

34:15.845 --> 34:18.306
Does this keep happening
because it's in the middle?

34:18.390 --> 34:22.185
-No way.
-When was your most recent kiss?

34:22.560 --> 34:24.271
It was within the past week, yes or no?

34:24.354 --> 34:25.647
[all mimicking drum roll]

34:25.730 --> 34:28.316
[Kim Wooju] Yes,
since we kissed before coming here.

34:28.817 --> 34:30.151
I'll drink.

34:30.235 --> 34:32.279
-[all exclaim]
-[Ms. Oh] What the heck?

34:32.988 --> 34:34.030
[Wonseok] Why...

34:34.114 --> 34:35.323
[Sejung] That's it?

34:36.366 --> 34:38.201
Ms. Yoo, you're no fun.

34:38.285 --> 34:39.536
[Wonseok] She loves beer a lot.

34:40.120 --> 34:41.663
-Is this bottom's up?
-[Sejung] Bottom's up.

34:41.746 --> 34:43.999
-Bottom's up!
-[all] Bottom's up!

34:44.082 --> 34:46.167
[all cheering]

34:46.251 --> 34:48.628
-[Ms. Oh] Mr. Kim can drink.
-[Wonseok] He's a heavy drinker.

35:00.890 --> 35:01.933
Mr. Kim.

35:04.394 --> 35:05.604
What's wrong?

35:05.687 --> 35:09.190
[inhales sharply] You pretended
to the very end not to have a boyfriend.

35:09.274 --> 35:12.444
That's because I haven't told Songhee yet.

35:12.527 --> 35:14.529
You kept hiding in the supermarket, too.

35:14.946 --> 35:17.032
Are you doing that
so you can go on blind dates?

35:17.115 --> 35:19.659
[chuckles] No way. Don't be silly.

35:20.118 --> 35:21.494
Why can't you say, then?

35:21.578 --> 35:24.080
"This man is my man.
This person is my person."

35:24.164 --> 35:25.540
Why can't you say so?

35:25.624 --> 35:28.335
How can I say that this man is my man?

35:29.085 --> 35:32.255
That he's so cute and so adorable
and that he drives me crazy?

35:32.339 --> 35:33.590
How can I say that?

35:33.673 --> 35:36.217
That would give everyone
the scare of a lifetime.

35:36.301 --> 35:37.594
[both chuckle softly]

35:38.845 --> 35:39.888
[gasps]

35:39.971 --> 35:41.139
[all exclaim, grunt]

35:41.222 --> 35:42.682
[♪ whimsical music playing]

35:43.308 --> 35:45.435
-What's wrong with you, Mr. Han?
-Sorry.

35:45.518 --> 35:46.895
[chuckles sheepishly]

35:46.978 --> 35:50.565
-What are you all doing there?
-You had to go and shove us.

35:50.649 --> 35:52.150
[stutters] Oh, well, I...

35:52.734 --> 35:54.027
I hurt my back. [clears throat]

35:54.736 --> 35:57.656
We saw it all already.

36:02.035 --> 36:03.536
Do you think this is enough?

36:03.620 --> 36:05.497
It'll last him three years.
That'll do. Let's go now.

36:08.291 --> 36:09.292
[Meri] You are sulking.

36:09.376 --> 36:12.379
-I'm not.
-Okay, buy everything you want.

36:12.462 --> 36:13.505
-What?
-[gasps]

36:14.547 --> 36:15.757
Don't we also need this?

36:17.300 --> 36:18.677
What are they doing?

36:19.094 --> 36:20.887
I think my heart is melting.

36:20.970 --> 36:22.389
What did I just witness?

36:22.472 --> 36:24.557
Ms. Yoo...

36:24.641 --> 36:27.811
-"Don't we also need this?"
-"Don't we also need this?"

36:31.272 --> 36:34.693
We played Truth or Dare
to see what you'd do.

36:35.694 --> 36:37.570
-[Meri] I feel humiliated.
-All that was on purpose?

36:37.654 --> 36:39.531
[Ms. Oh] We caught you red-handed.

36:39.614 --> 36:41.866
[Sejung giggles] Come back upstairs.

36:41.950 --> 36:43.952
You can't hide
from us any longer.

36:44.744 --> 36:45.954
-Come in.
-Come in.

36:46.037 --> 36:47.706
That's not how I did it.

36:50.083 --> 36:51.126
Ms. Yoo.

36:51.626 --> 36:54.003
Honestly.

36:54.421 --> 36:56.089
How could you?

36:56.172 --> 36:58.466
You should've told me at least.

36:58.550 --> 37:02.470
I messed up the timing
because I wanted to tell you first.

37:02.554 --> 37:04.639
-Liar.
-It's the truth.

37:04.723 --> 37:07.058
Well, to be honest,

37:07.517 --> 37:11.563
anyone with any amount of wit
would've caught on.

37:11.646 --> 37:12.772
What?

37:15.066 --> 37:17.068
I saw them.

37:17.152 --> 37:18.403
On the staircase at work.

37:18.903 --> 37:21.740
Getting up to no good.

37:22.115 --> 37:24.200
Yes, Mom.

37:24.284 --> 37:26.119
It's a dating show called I Am Single.

37:26.202 --> 37:28.747
I met with the producers.
Your son will be on TV.

37:30.457 --> 37:31.583
[exclaims]

37:31.666 --> 37:33.209
I have to go, Mom. Bye.

37:33.543 --> 37:34.586
[line disconnects]

37:36.588 --> 37:37.630
[whispers] What's that?

37:38.590 --> 37:40.175
[Meri] Seriously, someone will see us.

37:40.592 --> 37:41.885
[Kim Wooju] Who cares?

37:41.968 --> 37:43.678
-It's our company.
-[Meri giggles]

37:44.763 --> 37:45.805
[Wonseok] That was crazy.

37:46.139 --> 37:47.390
[Songhee chuckling]

37:48.016 --> 37:49.184
My blood pressure...

37:49.267 --> 37:50.643
This is insane.

37:50.727 --> 37:53.354
-They did make it obvious.
-[Wonseok] Pretty obvious.

37:53.438 --> 37:54.647
[Sejung] When did it all begin?

37:55.106 --> 37:57.066
Was it since then?

37:57.150 --> 37:59.277
Our first team dinner?

37:59.527 --> 38:01.571
-Let's go.
-No, I think...

38:02.155 --> 38:04.824
Where do you live? I'll drop you off.

38:05.408 --> 38:08.203
Get in. We'll be going then.

38:08.286 --> 38:10.705
Goodbye. [chuckles softly]

38:10.914 --> 38:13.166
[Ms. Oh] That's it. You two back then.

38:13.249 --> 38:15.460
-Didn't he drive her back?
-[Wonseok] That was it, then.

38:15.543 --> 38:17.504
-No, it wasn't then.
-[Songhee] Hang on.

38:17.587 --> 38:20.006
The couple Sejung said she saw
at the photo studio.

38:20.089 --> 38:21.382
You were the bride and groom?

38:22.300 --> 38:23.343
Mr. Kim?

38:24.135 --> 38:25.178
[gasps softly]

38:26.387 --> 38:27.514
[Sejung gasps]

38:27.597 --> 38:29.265
[♪ upbeat dreamy music playing]

38:29.349 --> 38:31.768
[stuttering] Did we do that?

38:32.143 --> 38:34.437
See? I was right, wasn't I?

38:34.521 --> 38:36.981
I swear I knew it was you
even from behind.

38:37.524 --> 38:39.442
The more we dig, the more we find.

38:39.859 --> 38:42.529
How long have you been hiding it from us?

38:42.612 --> 38:44.823
You two. When was the first time?

38:44.906 --> 38:47.617
-When was it?
-Yes, when was it?

38:47.700 --> 38:51.204
Well, it's a really long story
if I were to relay our whole history.

38:51.663 --> 38:52.664
[inhales deeply]

38:52.747 --> 38:55.333
Was I eight or nine years old then?

38:56.793 --> 38:57.919
[young Meri] Take it.

38:58.002 --> 39:00.338
My dad gave it to me on my birthday.

39:00.964 --> 39:02.465
[♪ ethereal sparkle]

39:02.549 --> 39:03.800
[both giggle softly]

39:05.552 --> 39:07.095
[all gasp in awe]

39:11.474 --> 39:15.436
Mr. Han, don't be jealous.
Be happy for them.

39:15.520 --> 39:18.273
Congratulations. We're happy for you,
so that's enough, please.

39:18.356 --> 39:19.858
-Cheers.
-[Wonseok] Congratulations.

39:19.941 --> 39:21.734
-[Songhee] Congratulations!
-[Kim Wooju] Thank you.

39:21.818 --> 39:25.405
-[Wonseok] Kiss!
-[all] Kiss!

39:25.488 --> 39:27.657
-Kiss! Right now!
-Kiss! Right away!

39:27.740 --> 39:29.826
-[Ms. Oh] Let's just drink.
-[Songhee] I got the chills.

39:31.077 --> 39:33.079
-[Sejung] That doesn't count. Do it again.
-[Ms. Oh chuckles]

39:36.457 --> 39:39.210
Do you know what I regret the most?

39:43.423 --> 39:44.465
Being patient with you.

39:45.633 --> 39:47.927
"He'll end it if I wait for him."

39:49.679 --> 39:51.014
"He'll come back to Mom."

39:51.556 --> 39:54.809
Eungsoo, I was duped, too.

39:55.685 --> 39:57.520
She blackmailed me into--

39:57.604 --> 39:59.856
Will you just stop it already?

40:01.524 --> 40:04.819
I've heard you on the phone with her
since I was 20 years old.

40:06.070 --> 40:08.573
Do you think I was clueless?

40:09.532 --> 40:10.575
Do you?

40:11.284 --> 40:12.327
[sighs in despair]

40:13.369 --> 40:14.954
[crying, breath trembling]

40:15.622 --> 40:18.333
Not only did you kill my uncle and aunt,

40:18.958 --> 40:21.085
but you went after Grandma, too.

40:22.003 --> 40:23.546
You're a monster.

40:23.630 --> 40:26.007
You don't know everything, Eungsoo.

40:26.090 --> 40:29.802
Do you know how your grandparents
and Wooju's family treated me?

40:30.345 --> 40:31.429
I did nothing wrong.

40:32.847 --> 40:33.890
I'm a victim, too.

40:35.099 --> 40:36.684
[♪ poignant, melancholy music playing]

40:38.603 --> 40:39.604
[scoffs]

40:41.856 --> 40:43.483
I hated myself

40:44.692 --> 40:47.946
because unlike you,
I was useless in school and at work.

40:50.114 --> 40:52.241
You have no idea
how relieved I am about that now.

40:54.243 --> 40:56.329
Don't call for Mom or me.

40:57.789 --> 40:58.998
I won't forgive you

41:00.083 --> 41:01.250
until the day I die.

41:03.169 --> 41:04.504
-[sniffles]
-Eungsoo.

41:06.089 --> 41:07.757
You can forget about me,

41:09.634 --> 41:12.387
but show some remorse
for what you did to Mom.

41:13.179 --> 41:14.222
Okay?

41:14.305 --> 41:16.099
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

41:16.641 --> 41:17.684
Eungsoo.

41:20.228 --> 41:21.437
I'll appeal.

41:23.606 --> 41:24.732
[sighs softly]

41:28.361 --> 41:30.822
Help me out. Eungsoo.

41:30.905 --> 41:32.198
Eungsoo. Eung...

41:44.502 --> 41:47.255
DONGBUK PENITENTIARY

41:50.717 --> 41:51.718
[sighs]

41:55.555 --> 41:56.597
[exhales]

41:58.766 --> 42:01.019
I'm hungry all of a sudden.

42:01.644 --> 42:04.689
Should we get something nice
since we're pretty far from home?

42:05.189 --> 42:06.232
I don't have an appetite.

42:07.025 --> 42:08.067
Okay.

42:09.277 --> 42:10.319
What would you like to eat?

42:11.779 --> 42:12.864
[chuckles softly]

42:12.947 --> 42:18.327
Well, I noticed a naengmyeon place
on the way here.

42:18.411 --> 42:20.413
There's also a pork cutlet place, and...

42:20.496 --> 42:22.790
There's a famous tofu hot pot place, Mom.

42:22.874 --> 42:23.875
Let's have malatang.

42:23.958 --> 42:25.001
Let's get malatang.

42:27.045 --> 42:28.087
Let's do that.

42:28.171 --> 42:30.089
[♪ soft, gentle music playing]

42:32.091 --> 42:33.551
-[sighs softly]
-[engine starts]

42:34.552 --> 42:36.095
Malatang it is.

42:42.477 --> 42:45.229
[news anchor over TV] Byeon Jongsik,
ex-mayor of Yongdu

42:45.313 --> 42:48.232
and possible presidential candidate,
is suspected of corruption.

42:48.316 --> 42:50.359
The report claims that Beauté Group

42:50.443 --> 42:53.780
lobbied him illegally to obtain
a department store license.

42:54.238 --> 42:56.741
This isn't a simple corruption scandal.

42:56.824 --> 43:01.037
It could cause a ripple that could affect
the whole presidential election.

43:01.954 --> 43:06.000
Let's hear from our correspondent
at the Supreme Prosecutors' Office.

43:06.084 --> 43:07.335
Kim Seokhyeon, are you there?

43:07.418 --> 43:10.421
[Seokhyeon] Prosecution believes
they have something

43:10.505 --> 43:12.715
that points to Beauté Group
paying Byeon a large sum.

43:12.799 --> 43:16.010
They obtained department store ledgers
and internal documents,

43:16.094 --> 43:19.597
and they're said to show funds
being sent to political circles.

43:19.680 --> 43:21.099
[Sungwoo] Father!

43:21.182 --> 43:22.975
-[exclaiming in pain]
-[muffled thudding]

43:23.059 --> 43:25.561
Not my face, Father. Don't hit my face.

43:26.020 --> 43:27.438
-My bones--
-You fool.

43:29.565 --> 43:32.068
-[thudding continues]
-[Sungwoo grunting]

43:32.193 --> 43:34.487
Father, wait. I'm really sorry.

43:36.697 --> 43:38.032
Father!

43:38.116 --> 43:39.784
[Sungwoo continues grunting]

43:39.867 --> 43:41.035
Father.

43:41.119 --> 43:42.370
[Sungwoo's dad] Are you kidding me?

43:42.453 --> 43:43.621
Oh, not my back.

43:43.704 --> 43:45.039
You got a bone just there.

43:45.123 --> 43:46.541
[groaning]

43:46.624 --> 43:48.126
[golf club clatters on floor]

43:52.922 --> 43:54.173
You asked to see me, sir?

44:02.890 --> 44:03.891
[door closes]

44:05.017 --> 44:06.269
[Sungwoo's dad] The mayor incident.

44:06.936 --> 44:08.688
You sort it out, Sanghyeon.

44:09.605 --> 44:11.107
You'll hear from a prosecutor.

44:11.190 --> 44:13.860
CEO'S OFFICE

44:13.943 --> 44:15.403
[♪ tense music playing]

44:28.791 --> 44:30.251
[children chattering]

44:37.175 --> 44:39.510
-[children] Hello.
-[Jingyeong] Hello.

44:41.053 --> 44:42.096
Hi.

44:42.763 --> 44:43.848
-[doctor 1] How cute.
-[doctor 2] They're so adorable.

44:43.931 --> 44:45.725
8TH DAEJU GENERAL HOSPITAL
COMMUNITY CARE DAY

44:45.808 --> 44:47.560
-[doctor 3] Say "ah."
-[kid] Four.

44:47.643 --> 44:49.478
-[doctor 3] It's somewhere here.
-[kid] Four.

44:49.979 --> 44:51.606
-[doctor 3] You have a cavity.
-[kid] Three.

44:52.940 --> 44:54.025
Bye.

44:56.194 --> 44:57.945
-Next.
-Hello.

44:58.029 --> 45:00.907
[Jingyeong] Hi,
will you roll up your sleeve?

45:08.247 --> 45:09.790
It'll sting just a little.

45:10.166 --> 45:11.626
A little prick.

45:11.709 --> 45:12.752
[liquid squirts]

45:14.337 --> 45:16.255
-That didn't hurt, did it?
-It hurt.

45:17.423 --> 45:20.301
Put up with it, then.
You should learn how.

45:21.010 --> 45:23.971
How will you manage out in the world
if you can't handle even this?

45:24.805 --> 45:29.560
Bear with it like you just did,
and you can meet a pretty girl like me.

45:29.644 --> 45:30.978
Okay? [giggles]

45:32.188 --> 45:34.065
Now hold onto this, okay?

45:34.148 --> 45:35.566
[children chattering]

45:49.121 --> 45:50.122
[sighs]

45:55.503 --> 45:56.879
[footsteps approaching]

45:56.963 --> 45:59.840
What's a busy man like you
doing here all of a sudden?

45:59.924 --> 46:03.177
I was passing by and thought of you,
so I got you something.

46:05.096 --> 46:06.597
What's this for?

46:07.306 --> 46:08.516
My birthday has already passed.

46:08.599 --> 46:10.726
Flowers aren't just for birthdays.

46:11.435 --> 46:15.189
You got me carnation flowers
each year on my birthday, Sanghyeon.

46:15.898 --> 46:18.609
You thanked me for raising you.

46:19.860 --> 46:24.657
As a kid, you stayed quietly in your room
unless you were getting into a fight.

46:24.740 --> 46:28.160
You have no idea how proud I am
to see how well you've grown.

46:30.288 --> 46:31.330
[inhales deeply]

46:31.414 --> 46:33.165
[♪ soft, sentimental music playing]

46:35.960 --> 46:37.962
I won't be able to visit for a while.

46:39.630 --> 46:42.633
So, I'm giving you
next year's flowers in advance.

46:43.175 --> 46:44.218
Why?

46:45.011 --> 46:46.637
Are you being transferred abroad again?

46:48.264 --> 46:49.307
Yes.

46:50.391 --> 46:51.684
Don't work so hard.

46:51.767 --> 46:53.311
You should be getting married.

46:54.103 --> 46:56.981
I'd like to see you
happily married with a family

46:57.606 --> 47:00.067
so I can finally relax. [chuckles softly]

47:01.694 --> 47:02.737
Here.

47:03.404 --> 47:04.447
It's chrysanthemum tea.

47:05.239 --> 47:07.074
I picked and dried the flowers.

47:07.158 --> 47:09.201
I put some aside to give you.

47:15.666 --> 47:16.709
Thank you.

47:18.002 --> 47:19.003
[knock at door]

47:19.378 --> 47:20.421
Come in.

47:25.343 --> 47:27.720
The doctors are done
and are ready to leave.

47:27.803 --> 47:28.846
Are they?

47:28.929 --> 47:30.139
I'll leave, then.

47:30.222 --> 47:31.599
You're leaving already?

47:31.682 --> 47:32.850
Why don't you stay for dinner?

47:33.100 --> 47:34.268
I should go.

47:34.352 --> 47:36.520
If something happens,
or you need something for the orphanage,

47:36.604 --> 47:38.689
call my company. I'll leave instructions.

47:47.573 --> 47:49.075
-[Sanghyeon] Look after yourself.
-I will.

47:49.617 --> 47:50.659
Thank you.

47:52.411 --> 47:54.205
-Watch your health.
-I will.

47:54.580 --> 47:55.623
I'll see you when you return.

47:55.706 --> 47:57.083
-Go on back inside.
-Okay.

48:00.544 --> 48:01.879
Mr. Baek!

48:07.426 --> 48:08.469
How...

48:09.095 --> 48:10.262
What are you doing here?

48:13.766 --> 48:15.559
MIJI'S SNACK FOODS

48:15.643 --> 48:17.770
[customer] Two tteokbokki, please.

48:17.853 --> 48:19.438
[waitress] Okay, grab a seat.

48:21.857 --> 48:23.943
-[Sanghyeon] I was really surprised.
-[Jingyeong] Right?

48:24.443 --> 48:26.862
-Here you go.
-[Sanghyeon] Thank you.

48:30.533 --> 48:32.201
-Enjoy yourselves.
-Thank you.

48:34.954 --> 48:38.541
A doctor who volunteered last year
insisted I try this place.

48:38.624 --> 48:41.335
I was going to come on my own
after we were done.

48:42.086 --> 48:44.338
You're lucky when it comes to free food.

48:44.422 --> 48:45.506
It's pretty spicy.

48:46.215 --> 48:47.675
How spicy can tteokbokki be?

48:54.890 --> 48:56.100
[hissing]

48:56.183 --> 48:57.268
[groans softly]

49:00.271 --> 49:01.564
[♪ upbeat, whimsical music playing]

49:01.647 --> 49:02.773
[chuckles softly]

49:03.190 --> 49:04.233
Drink this.

49:06.110 --> 49:07.403
You know what to do.

49:11.699 --> 49:13.033
Have you been here before?

49:15.369 --> 49:16.620
Until I finished middle school,

49:17.663 --> 49:19.123
this place held many memories for me.

49:19.623 --> 49:22.460
[hums thoughtfully] You used to live here.

49:22.543 --> 49:24.086
I grew up in that orphanage.

49:24.545 --> 49:25.713
[exclaims in realization]

49:26.422 --> 49:30.217
That's why Mother Superior
gave you something.

49:30.593 --> 49:32.887
I wondered why you got special treatment.

49:34.263 --> 49:35.890
-You don't seem surprised.
-[slurps]

49:36.682 --> 49:38.434
[exhales, hisses]

49:38.517 --> 49:39.518
[groans]

49:39.894 --> 49:42.188
This heat is way more shocking than that.

49:43.606 --> 49:45.149
Hang on. [hissing]

49:46.609 --> 49:48.235
Now you can ask. [panting]

49:48.319 --> 49:50.279
-I'll act really surprised.
-[chuckles softly]

49:50.988 --> 49:52.490
[♪ soft, gentle music playing]

49:52.990 --> 49:54.909
You're pretty unusual.

49:55.826 --> 49:56.869
Me?

49:57.870 --> 49:59.997
No, I'm completely [in English] normal.

50:00.915 --> 50:02.500
[in Korean] You're the unusual one.

50:02.583 --> 50:04.919
You're way too serious.

50:05.461 --> 50:07.046
Do you think it's a cool look?

50:07.755 --> 50:10.007
Relax your face and smile a bit.

50:10.758 --> 50:12.009
If smiling's too hard...

50:13.928 --> 50:17.181
Pick one day
and laugh all you can every week.

50:17.765 --> 50:18.807
How's that?

50:20.100 --> 50:21.143
[chuckles softly]

50:21.227 --> 50:22.311
[Jingyeong chuckles]

50:23.479 --> 50:24.855
If that's weird, too...

50:25.606 --> 50:26.649
Well,

50:27.107 --> 50:30.319
why don't you call me once a week?

50:31.028 --> 50:32.071
I'll make you laugh.

50:37.993 --> 50:40.287
I told you this place
held many memories for me.

50:40.371 --> 50:41.455
Yes.

50:41.539 --> 50:45.376
The owner once reported me for theft.

50:50.130 --> 50:53.968
She'd taken off her gold ring to work,
and it had disappeared.

50:54.051 --> 50:58.097
So, she searched all the kids' bags.

50:58.556 --> 50:59.598
The ring

51:00.391 --> 51:02.476
happened to be right by my feet.

51:06.438 --> 51:10.067
The thief had dropped it
so he wouldn't get caught.

51:10.150 --> 51:11.360
I was named

51:12.736 --> 51:13.821
as the thief.

51:13.904 --> 51:15.614
You were framed?

51:17.491 --> 51:18.534
I denied it was me.

51:20.035 --> 51:21.078
I said it wasn't.

51:23.455 --> 51:25.541
Just then, someone yelled from behind me.

51:27.334 --> 51:29.545
"He's an orphan."

51:30.462 --> 51:31.797
"He's from the orphanage."

51:35.342 --> 51:40.389
That's when everyone
started to call me a thief.

51:41.056 --> 51:42.057
I decided then

51:43.434 --> 51:45.019
that I should

51:47.146 --> 51:48.439
leave the orphanage.

51:51.442 --> 51:52.484
What then?

51:53.485 --> 51:54.695
What happened next?

51:54.778 --> 51:56.071
The actual thief.

51:57.364 --> 51:59.074
I moved into his house.

51:59.617 --> 52:00.743
I kept my mouth shut.

52:01.994 --> 52:03.537
I took exams for him,

52:04.288 --> 52:06.415
and in return, I had a comfortable life.

52:07.875 --> 52:08.917
Sometimes...

52:10.210 --> 52:13.088
I got punished for him, too.

52:14.131 --> 52:15.799
[♪ soft, melancholy music playing]

52:15.883 --> 52:17.468
Once I switched environments...

52:19.219 --> 52:20.346
[sighs deeply]

52:20.429 --> 52:25.809
people stopped looking down on me.

52:27.144 --> 52:28.729
They didn't suspect me, either.

52:29.438 --> 52:30.481
So what now?

52:33.067 --> 52:34.443
Are you repaying the favor

52:35.736 --> 52:37.196
to the actual ring thief?

52:37.571 --> 52:38.614
Continuously?

52:39.823 --> 52:42.451
Why? For a comfortable life?

52:46.872 --> 52:49.375
I just don't want to go back
to how things were.

52:51.126 --> 52:53.754
Even so, you can't...

52:57.883 --> 52:58.926
Hang on.

53:04.223 --> 53:06.016
Why are you telling me this?

53:07.559 --> 53:08.602
[chuckles softly]

53:09.311 --> 53:10.354
I don't know.

53:13.565 --> 53:15.442
I guess I wanted to come clean

53:17.277 --> 53:18.445
to you, at least.

53:18.946 --> 53:19.988
What?

53:22.074 --> 53:23.200
[chuckles]

53:27.121 --> 53:28.122
[Jingyeong exclaims]

53:34.586 --> 53:35.629
Let's eat.

53:36.922 --> 53:38.298
You should eat, too.

53:40.759 --> 53:41.844
It's really spicy.

53:41.927 --> 53:44.304
How spicy can tteokbokki be?

53:45.973 --> 53:47.057
It's spicy, isn't it?

53:47.599 --> 53:49.184
-[coughs, clears throat]
-[laughing]

53:51.395 --> 53:52.479
Drink this.

53:52.563 --> 53:53.564
COOL JUICY
PEACH FLAVOR

53:54.440 --> 53:55.733
[hissing]

53:55.816 --> 53:57.901
-It really is spicy.
-[chuckles]

53:58.026 --> 53:59.778
[ship horn blares]

54:00.404 --> 54:01.405
[gulping]

54:03.866 --> 54:05.200
-[exhales]
-[phone vibrates]

54:07.619 --> 54:08.662
[sighs softly]

54:09.413 --> 54:11.707
[recruiter] Mr. Kim. Thank you
for applying to our company

54:11.790 --> 54:14.251
and showing us your passion.

54:14.710 --> 54:17.546
I'm sorry we can't offer you
a position this time.

54:18.046 --> 54:20.132
I hope to cross paths with you again.

54:20.215 --> 54:21.258
[phone vibrates]

54:21.341 --> 54:24.970
THIS IS ONNURI CAPITAL
WE CANNOT HIRE YOU AT THIS TIME

54:25.679 --> 54:26.847
[phone vibrates]

54:26.930 --> 54:28.265
[♪ whimsical music playing]

54:31.185 --> 54:32.186
[sighs wearily]

54:42.321 --> 54:43.739
[sighs]

54:45.240 --> 54:46.283
Meri.

54:47.034 --> 54:48.660
The tie you got me,

54:49.495 --> 54:51.288
and the suit and shoes.

54:55.792 --> 54:58.045
They're not as effective without you.

55:02.508 --> 55:03.800
When you were there,

55:05.552 --> 55:06.762
I aced every interview.

55:21.652 --> 55:23.695
[driver] We're here, sir.

55:23.946 --> 55:25.697
[snoring softly]

55:25.781 --> 55:26.949
Sir?

55:27.866 --> 55:29.743
-We're here.
-What?

55:31.787 --> 55:32.871
[seatbelt button clicks]

55:52.349 --> 55:53.725
Why did I come here?

56:02.276 --> 56:03.277
[chuckles softly]

56:05.571 --> 56:06.655
[gate clatters]

56:17.666 --> 56:19.167
[♪ dramatic guitar music playing]

56:43.984 --> 56:45.193
[exclaims]

56:45.485 --> 56:46.695
I'll take that for you.

56:47.863 --> 56:49.364
-[grunts]
-[chuckles softly]

56:49.448 --> 56:50.490
Wait.

56:51.950 --> 56:53.118
Is this all your clothes?

56:53.201 --> 56:54.953
No, the rest are upstairs.

56:55.621 --> 56:57.247
I'll be here until the weekend,

56:57.331 --> 56:59.374
so I'll pack my pajamas
and bed covers later.

56:59.458 --> 57:01.418
You said your sister
lived in a studio apartment.

57:01.501 --> 57:03.170
Is there room for all this?

57:03.253 --> 57:05.172
My place is way more spacious.

57:05.255 --> 57:06.506
We can handle this much.

57:06.590 --> 57:08.175
Oh, can you?

57:08.967 --> 57:10.552
I'm the only one who's sad about this.

57:11.011 --> 57:12.054
What do you mean?

57:12.137 --> 57:15.474
If you move in with your sister...

57:18.810 --> 57:19.978
[clicks tongue] Never mind.

57:21.480 --> 57:23.815
-Where are you walking off to?
-Leave me alone.

57:24.191 --> 57:25.275
[Meri exclaiming]

57:25.901 --> 57:28.153
I want to stick close to you
like this, too.

57:29.196 --> 57:30.280
Don't do this.

57:30.364 --> 57:31.573
I will do this.

57:32.366 --> 57:33.533
[both chuckle]

57:35.619 --> 57:36.787
[chuckles]

57:36.912 --> 57:38.705
Just move in with me.

57:39.498 --> 57:40.749
I can't do that.

57:40.832 --> 57:41.875
[sighs wearily]

57:41.958 --> 57:43.710
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

57:44.711 --> 57:46.505
My place has way more room.

57:48.173 --> 57:49.925
-[both chuckle]
-Do you want to stay the night?

57:50.884 --> 57:51.927
-Tonight?
-Yes.

57:52.010 --> 57:53.553
-[Kim Wooju] Yes.
-[giggling]

57:54.888 --> 57:56.056
[sighs softly]

57:56.139 --> 57:57.849
[♪ music crescendos, fades]

58:02.479 --> 58:03.689
[birds chirping]

58:09.319 --> 58:10.862
[phone alarm ringing]

58:22.749 --> 58:23.917
[Kim Wooju] Sleep in.

58:24.668 --> 58:25.836
I need to get to work.

58:26.128 --> 58:28.004
Get ready quicker later.

58:28.088 --> 58:29.214
[chuckles]

58:31.675 --> 58:33.510
[Kim Wooju sighs contentedly, chuckles]

58:33.593 --> 58:35.554
[♪ enthralling orchestral music playing]

59:16.136 --> 59:17.554
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

59:21.892 --> 59:23.393
-You're up.
-[chuckles softly]

59:24.728 --> 59:25.812
What's all this?

59:26.688 --> 59:28.023
You eat breakfast.

59:28.106 --> 59:29.232
[Meri gasps]

59:30.150 --> 59:32.611
-[chuckles softly]
-You remembered that?

59:32.986 --> 59:34.112
Did you go out?

59:34.196 --> 59:36.031
Yes, to our cafeteria.

59:36.490 --> 59:37.574
[egg taps against pan]

59:38.116 --> 59:40.577
You said you needed hot coffee to wake up.

59:40.660 --> 59:42.078
[Meri exclaims contentedly]

59:43.413 --> 59:44.414
[chuckles softly]

59:44.706 --> 59:45.832
What?

59:46.875 --> 59:48.835
Well, this really feels
like we're newlyweds.

59:48.919 --> 59:50.796
We are newlyweds.

59:51.338 --> 59:53.590
You only get this kind of service
in the honeymoon phase.

59:54.299 --> 59:55.509
[exclaims sarcastically]

59:56.593 --> 59:59.638
Is what they say,
but I'll keep cooking for you.

59:59.721 --> 01:00:00.847
Until when?

01:00:01.431 --> 01:00:04.559
[hums thoughtfully]
Until egg yolks turn green?

01:00:04.643 --> 01:00:06.269
-What does that mean?
-No.

01:00:06.728 --> 01:00:09.689
[hums thoughtfully]
Until my hair turns white?

01:00:15.946 --> 01:00:17.113
Forever?

01:00:17.197 --> 01:00:18.782
-Forever.
-[giggles]

01:00:19.699 --> 01:00:20.867
Eat up and get ready.

01:00:22.828 --> 01:00:24.037
I'll scramble the egg.

01:00:24.371 --> 01:00:25.914
[Meri] I wanted it fried.

01:00:30.168 --> 01:00:31.419
Do you finish late today?

01:00:31.962 --> 01:00:33.004
Probably?

01:00:33.088 --> 01:00:34.422
I'll work late, too, then.

01:00:34.506 --> 01:00:36.633
What for? Go home early and rest.

01:00:37.092 --> 01:00:38.218
It's boring on my own.

01:00:41.179 --> 01:00:42.430
-I'll call you later.
-Okay.

01:00:45.016 --> 01:00:46.059
Bye.

01:00:53.441 --> 01:00:54.901
[phone vibrating]

01:00:57.487 --> 01:00:58.780
KIM WOOJU

01:01:09.958 --> 01:01:11.209
[line ringing]

01:01:12.252 --> 01:01:15.255
[automated voice] The call cannot
be connected. Transferring to voicemail.

01:01:16.339 --> 01:01:17.424
MERI

01:01:17.799 --> 01:01:19.301
Is this how you want it to be?

01:01:22.804 --> 01:01:24.014
[phone clatters on desk]

01:01:24.097 --> 01:01:25.098
[mouse clicks]

01:01:29.060 --> 01:01:31.187
PRESS CONFERENCE:
MYUNGSOONDANG HEIR'S FRAUD EXPOSED

01:01:33.982 --> 01:01:35.066
[email notification pings]

01:01:35.317 --> 01:01:36.359
What?

01:01:36.443 --> 01:01:40.238
"Fourth-generation heir of Myungsoondang
Kim Wooju's fraud scandal?"

01:01:41.323 --> 01:01:42.782
-[keyboard clacking]
-[phone vibrates]

01:01:42.866 --> 01:01:43.909
[man] Hurry up.

01:01:44.951 --> 01:01:46.620
"Myungsoondang Kim Wooju."

01:01:46.703 --> 01:01:47.746
[♪ tense music playing]

01:01:47.829 --> 01:01:49.789
-Myungsoondang, press conference.
-A press conference?

01:01:50.916 --> 01:01:52.167
THE PUBLIC HAS A RIGHT TO KNOW...

01:01:52.250 --> 01:01:53.668
[keyboard clacking]

01:01:56.004 --> 01:01:57.047
SEND

01:02:07.849 --> 01:02:08.934
[sighs]

01:02:14.522 --> 01:02:15.523
[phone pings]

01:02:17.359 --> 01:02:18.652
KIM WOOJU

01:02:18.735 --> 01:02:20.654
PRESS CONFERENCE:
MYUNGSOONDANG HEIR'S FRAUD EXPOSED

01:02:23.990 --> 01:02:26.743
SEPT 5, 2025, 10 A.M.
2ND FLOOR, CENTRAL SQUARE BUSINESS HOTEL

01:02:26.826 --> 01:02:28.662
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

01:02:43.593 --> 01:02:44.886
[phone ringing]

01:02:47.764 --> 01:02:48.807
[chuckles]

01:02:49.516 --> 01:02:51.267
You called because you miss me already?

01:02:51.351 --> 01:02:52.894
[Meri] Something happened, Wooju.

01:02:55.438 --> 01:02:56.690
[reporter 1] Yes.

01:02:56.773 --> 01:02:58.608
-I'm on the way now.
-[reporter 2] Get moving!

01:02:59.442 --> 01:03:01.361
-[reporter 3] Yes, I'm here.
-[reporter 4] Get inside!

01:03:01.444 --> 01:03:02.779
[reporters clamoring]

01:03:05.824 --> 01:03:09.744
MYUNGSOONDANG'S 4TH-GEN SUCCESSOR
KIM WOOJU'S TRUE COLORS

01:03:09.828 --> 01:03:11.454
[camera shutters clicking rapidly]

01:03:13.623 --> 01:03:14.916
MYUNGSOONDANG HEIR'S FRAUD EXPOSED

01:03:15.000 --> 01:03:17.252
I greet all you respectable journalists.

01:03:17.335 --> 01:03:20.922
I'm Kim Wooju,
an ordinary man who lives in Seoul.

01:03:26.720 --> 01:03:28.304
I stand here today

01:03:28.722 --> 01:03:30.557
to expose the successor
of a mid-sized company

01:03:30.640 --> 01:03:33.351
for breaking up a family with his affairs

01:03:33.435 --> 01:03:36.354
and attempt to make
an illegal profit of millions.

01:03:36.438 --> 01:03:37.939
I believe his immoral and unjust act

01:03:39.774 --> 01:03:40.942
must come out.

01:03:42.318 --> 01:03:43.361
What?

01:03:43.903 --> 01:03:44.946
A press conference?

01:03:49.784 --> 01:03:51.119
[♪ music increases in tempo]

01:03:51.202 --> 01:03:52.620
[tires screeching]

01:04:01.546 --> 01:04:03.840
[♪ gentle, poignant pop music playing]

01:04:30.200 --> 01:04:32.202
Translated by Jennifer Jean Lim
